    "question": {
      ":question/id": "fd522a3e-ce03-5652-acaa-708366cf408f",
      ":question/problem": "At which points on the curve $x^{2} + 2 x y=3 - 4 y$ is the tangent vector to the curve perpendicular to the vector $j$?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.\n\n- **I.** $(-3,1)$\n- **II.** $(-3,3)$\n- **III.** $(- \\frac{3}{2},3)$\n- **IV.** $(-1,1)$\n- **V.** $(-1,3)$\n- **VI.** $(1,1)$\n- **VII.** $(3,-3)$",
